  "generated_text": "To find the measure of the hypotenuse of a right triangle with leg lengths of 75 and 100 units, we can use the Pythagorean theorem. The Pythagorean theorem states that in a right triangle, the square of the length of the hypotenuse is equal to the sum of the squares of the lengths of the other two legs.\n\nLet's denote the length of the hypotenuse by \\( c \\). According to the Pythagorean theorem:\n\\[\nc^2 = 75^2 + 100^2\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the squares of the legs:\n\\[\n75^2 = 5625\n\\]\n\\[\n100^2 = 10000\n\\]\n\nNext, we add these squares together:\n\\[\n5625 + 10000 = 15625\n\\]\n\nNow, we take the square root of both sides to find \\( c \\):\n\\[\nc = \\sqrt{15625} = 125\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of the hypotenuse is \\(\\boxed{125}\\).",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[125, '125']",
    "gold_answer": "Using the Pythagorean Theorem, \\begin{align*}\nd&=\\sqrt{75^2+100^2} \\\\\n&=\\sqrt{25^2(3^2+4^2)} \\\\\n&=25\\sqrt{3^2+4^2} \\\\\n&=25\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\\n&=25\\sqrt{25} \\\\\n&=25 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=\\boxed{125} \\text{units}\n\\end{align*}",
    "is_correct": true
  },
